# The review layer (src/review) keeps notes on this device unless two things are true:
#   - both Supabase values below are set when the site is built, and
#   - the visitor opened Riley's review link, which carries the review key.
# Then notes are shared live with everyone holding the link ("Live" in the review bar).
#
# The review key, in two lines:
#   1. Make a long random key (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) and insert it with the template at the end of supabase/review.sql.
#   2. Send the review link with it: https://…/truemark/#/review?key=<the key>
# The key is never put in this file or in the site's code; the link carries it.
#
# Create the tables and functions first with supabase/review.sql. Copy this file to .env.local and fill it in.

# Project Settings -> API -> Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklmnop.supabase.co
VITE_REVIEW_SUPABASE_URL=

# Project Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> anon / public. It is meant to be public: it can
# call the review functions, and they refuse anyone without the review key.
VITE_REVIEW_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The name notes kept on this device carry. Shared notes take their review from the key instead.
VITE_REVIEW_PROJECT=truemark
